history_merged_on_consolidation.description:
You moved **{dropped}** into the same location as **{kept}**, and both had been recording the same {count} entities. Home Assistant allows only one entity per sensor reading, so the merged location keeps the entity belonging to the receiver that was added first ({kept}) and the duplicate copies from {dropped} were removed along with their recorded history.

The readings themselves are not lost: the surviving entities now record whichever receiver receives the sensor. Only the second, duplicate copy of the history is gone.

Removed: {entities}
